+# TB-FIN-01C / TB-08-R2-R5-R5-R1 — installed qualification
+
+Parent source tree `d3283d5038590d34deb4cdaf3c0b4cba4a1e44db` restored from the R5-R5 archive and verified using Git's tree hash. No production runtime, policy, service deadline or graphical authorization implementation changes. Qualification-only changes: warm harness readiness observation waits up to the existing 120-second production allowance (rather than 20 seconds); other harness response waits 30 seconds. Actual production watchdog 30 seconds, snapshot freshness 30 seconds and synchronous permit 2 seconds unchanged.
+
+## Accepted evidence
+
+* Offline Debian 13 QEMU guest, systemd PID 1, cgroup v2, loopback only, pinned Python 3.12.16/Freqtrade 2026.10. Actual independent identities and native signed wallet. Both transient systemd controlled-book scenarios pass 8/8 checkpoints each and exit zero; warm readiness 18.608 s (expiry), 18.774 s (checkpoint). Expiry uses logical clock in this fixture; checkpoint really advances through independent adoption/revocation. Entries and settlement use actual Freqtrade PAPER persistence, not public-market data. Each verifies retained runtime, protection, reservation held until authenticated evidence, no duplicate entry or settlement, clean lease close.
+* Focused seven graphical and five protection tests pass on pinned host runtime. No claim of a new full regression run; parent had 498 passed, two optional skips.
+* Actual named native service in a new disposable guest passes wall-clock expiry: readiness without snapshot in 23 s, Type=notify, cgroup membership and live 30 s watchdog. Actual named relay, desk broker and terminal settlement units, controlled market fixture with root-owned temporary ExecStart override; no live exchange or production network constructor. Native wallet admission, one actual PAPER trade/two orders, same PID, signed snapshot ages for 32 seconds, protected exit on retained grant, held reservation until renewed signed snapshot; exactly one authenticated release, $100 principal and $4.8951 simulated protected gain, no remaining exposure or pending amount, zero restarts. Exit zero. Cleanup pauses disposable desk, stops units and removes overrides. Disk checks on completed guests pass; original base hash unchanged.
+* Actual named graphical service definition verifies. Wrong identity refused; dedicated approval UID without active trusted local X11 session refused with expected reason; direct installed service startup fails without that session, zero PID and no pending approval. Does not qualify positive graphical approval or polkit interaction. No trusted graphical seat was provisioned; prior R5-R4 isolated GUI acceptance remains scoped to that fixture.
+
+## Harness flaws corrected and remaining qualification
+
+First named run checked watchdog effectiveness while inactive (systemd reported infinity); assertion moved to live service. No production unit change. First named checkpoint test failed at synthetic reserve adoption, before any order, after successful readiness and negative graphical checks. Corrected synthetic test preparation includes risk policy, draft, signed wallet and exact independent review prerequisites. The result of the retry is recorded below. Checkpoint production named-service acceptance is distinct from the two successful transient tests. Real local unlocked X11 approval seat and positive polkit/desktop lifecycle, public-market full native startup and sustained PAPER, migrated goals, forward validation and credential-security acceptance remain required. No actual desk, main, CI or LIVE change.
+
+## Named checkpoint retry — PASS
+
+Fresh disposable guest; corrected harness independently adopted a synthetic reserve policy through the named authority, then admitted actual PAPER entry. With one open order and snapshot publication stopped, independently reviewed revocation advanced the actual witness, the still-unexpired signed snapshot was refused with `snapshot_checkpoint_changed`, and the retained native PID reduced the existing exposure. Reservation remained held until a fresh authenticated snapshot, after which exact single settlement passed. Two orders, $100 principal and $4.8951 simulated protected gain, no remaining exposure/pending/reservation, zero restarts. `NAMED_SERVICE_EXIT=0`; cleanup and graceful poweroff completed. Final child disk check clean and immutable base hash unchanged. Checkpoint protection is accepted in the named-service controlled-book fixture; no positive production desktop or live trading acceptance claimed. First expiry trial's executed harness preceded the addition of checkpoint mode; evidence includes the executed expiry shell and final combined harness. The positive independent approvals here used synthetic exact-review credentials under the independently installed authority, not a genuine graphical session.
